Version 4.11, May 12, 2016

5/4/16   [EDGcpfe/17147]
Undefined behavior in std::initializer_list<T>::end

Previously, the implementation of std::initializer_list<T>::end provided with
the front end returned the expression

    this->__array + this->__length

which technically resulted in undefined behavior for empty initializer lists,
where __array is a null pointer and __length is zero.  This is now fixed.


