Version 4.6, March 30, 2013

12/7/12 [EDGcpfe/13489,EDGcpfe/9247,EDGcpfe/9975]
C++11: add std::bad_array_new_length and __cxa_throw_bad_array_new_length

The std::bad_array_new_length class (thrown when the number of elements in an
array new operation is invalid) has been added to the new.stdh include file.
In the IA-64 ABI, __cxa_throw_bad_array_new_length has also been added
(which unconditionally throws an object of type std::bad_array_new_length).


